"""SM05B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN) - JST SH 5-pin 1.00 mm side-entry SMD header. Bare part.

Datasheet: JST SH connector catalogue (eSH.pdf, URL in pcb.toml). Specifications (p1): 1.0 A
(AWG #28), 50 V AC/DC, -25 to +85 C including temperature rise, 20 mOhm contact resistance
initial; AWG #32 to #28 wire. Header table (p3): SM05B-SRSS-TB, A = 4.0 mm (pin 1 to pin 5),
B = 7.0 mm body width, 4.25 mm body depth, 2.9 mm high; tin-plated contacts and reinforcement.
Mates with the SHR-05V-S(-B) housing (p2, B = 6.0 / 8.0 mm).

Footprint: the side-entry PC board layout of p1: five 0.6 x 1.55 mm contact pads on a 1.00 mm
pitch, two 1.2 x 1.8 mm reinforcement pads (MP) whose inner edges sit 0.7 mm beyond the outer
contacts, 5.55 mm from the far edge of the reinforcement pads to the far edge of the contacts
and 4.0 mm to their near edge. KiCad library footprint
JST_SH_SM05B-SRSS-TB_1x05-1MP_P1.00mm_Horizontal with its STEP embedded; the mating face is
on the reinforcement-pad side (+Y), 0.2 mm inside the pads' outer edge (p1 "(0.2)").

The reinforcement pads are tin-plated metal tabs with no contact function (p3 "Reinforcement");
MP exposes them so the board can tie them to a net (usually GND) or leave them unconnected.
"""

prefix = config(str, default="P", help="Reference designator prefix")

P1 = io(Net)
P2 = io(Net)
P3 = io(Net)
P4 = io(Net)
P5 = io(Net)
MP = io(Net)

Component(
    name="HEADER",
    prefix=prefix,
    symbol=Symbol(library="SM05B-SRSS-TB.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("JST_SH_SM05B-SRSS-TB_1x05-1MP_P1.00mm_Horizontal.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="SM05B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN)", manufacturer="JST"),
    pins={"1": P1, "2": P2, "3": P3, "4": P4, "5": P5, "MP": MP},
    type="connector",
)
